{title: Hiding in Thee}
{artist: William O. Cushing / Ira D. Sankey}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 125}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Broadman Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: Broadman Press, 1940), # 129)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]O safe to the Rock that is [C7]high[Bb]er [C7]than [F]I,
[F]My [Bb]soul__[F]__ in its conflicts and [C]sor[F]rows would [C7]fly;
[C7]So [F]sinful, so weary, Thine, [C7]Thine, [Bb]would [C7]I [F]be;
[F]Thou [Bb]blest__[F]__ Rock of Ages, [Dm]I’m [F]hid[Am]ing__[C]__ in [F]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C7]Hiding in Thee, [F]hiding in Thee,
[F]Thou blest Rock of Ages, I’m hid[C]ing in [F]Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]In the calm of the noontide, in [C7]sor[Bb]row’s [C7]lone [F]hour,
[F]In [Bb]times__[F]__ when temptation casts [C]o’er [F]me its [C7]power;
[C7]In the [F]tempests of life, on its [C7]wide, [Bb]heav[C7]ing [F]sea,
[F]Thou [Bb]blest__[F]__ “Rock of Ages,” [Dm]I’m [F]hid[Am]ing__[C]__ in [F]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]How oft in the conflict, when [C7]pressed [Bb]by [C7]the [F]foe,
[F]I have [Bb]fled__[F]__ to my Refuge and [C]breathed [F]out my [C7]woe;
[C7]How [F]often, when trials like [C7]sea [Bb]bil[C7]lows [F]roll,
[F]Have I [Bb]hid__[F]__den in Thee, O [Dm]Thou [F]rock [Am]of__[C]__ my [F]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
